.venv

# Token POINTER backups written by switch_singleton_token.sh / lane token flips. The live
# pointers are ignored above; the .bak copies were not, so a `git add -A` would commit them.
# They contain PATHS (not token material) but still do not belong in the repo.
*_default_token.bak-*
.*_default_token.bak-*

# ============================================================================
# VPS-migration gate half (b) — keep runtime state & session junk out of git so
# the orch->gzb host move (op17195/17198) drops nothing real and sweeps in no
# secrets. (Nazim/console, 2026-08-27.)
# ============================================================================
# Per-lane/body MODEL pointers (which model each lane runs) — runtime state set
# at boot by scripts/fleet_model.sh; machine-local, never versioned. .fleet_model
# was historically tracked; untracked (git rm --cached) in this same change.
.*_model
.*_model.bak*
# Secret token-pointer variants not already covered above (e.g. the
# .nazim_default_token.was.<...> preswitch snapshot). SECRET — handle by name only.
.*_default_token*
*_default_token*
# Handoff/backup snapshots under reports/ — transient, regenerated each session.
reports/*.bak
reports/*.bak-*
# Session scratchpad (bus_send.py etc. — recreated per session, handoff pattern).
scratchpad/
# Runtime watchdog/probe/dashboard state (regenerated at boot; host-local).
state/ci_orphan_watchdog.json
state/opus_reprobe_storefront.json
state/cosem_dashboard_msg_id
# Broaden the PII/residency block to ALL depths under reports/ (the top-level-only
# reports/*.png globs missed subdir artifacts — screenshots, client namelists,
# result spreadsheets). Client PII/media must NEVER reach git, and MUST NOT ride a
# git-borne host move onto gzb (cross-client isolation). (gate half b, 2026-08-27.)
reports/**/*.png
reports/**/*.jpg
reports/**/*.jpeg
reports/**/*.gif
reports/**/*.webp
reports/**/*.pdf
reports/**/*.pptx
reports/**/*.ppt
reports/**/*.csv
reports/**/*.xlsx
reports/**/*.xls
reports/**/*.docx
reports/**/*.doc
reports/**/*.zip
reports/**/*.db
reports/**/*.sqlite
